This function lists everyone whose balance exceeds a limit. Note the Java tell: looping over .keys() and then indexing back into the dict for each value.

    def flag_overdue(balances, limit):
        flagged = []
        for name in balances.keys():
            if balances[name] > limit:
                flagged.append(name)
        return flagged

Rewrite it idiomatically in solution.py; same name, same behavior. (Hint: .items() gives you key and value together — no balances[name] lookup anywhere.)
